Statements about the work, not part of its discourse — titles, contributors, provenance, and configuration.

<section #ag-abstract | `<abstract>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<abstract>`.

<code-block #code:ag-abstract-1>
<abstract |
This paper presents new evidence that elephant populations
significantly affect regional climate patterns through their
role in shaping vegetation and carbon storage.
>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-abstract-1>
<abstract |
This paper presents new evidence that elephant populations
significantly affect regional climate patterns through their
role in shaping vegetation and carbon storage.
>
</minipage>

*Unstructured abstract (the default). Single paragraph of summary prose.*

<section #ag-affiliation | `<affiliation>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<affiliation>`.

<code-block #code:ag-affiliation-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
  <affiliation | Anthropic>
</author>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-affiliation-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
  <affiliation | Anthropic>
</author>
</minipage>

*Simple author affiliation. The affiliation sits as a sub-element
of &lt;author&gt;, parallel to other rich-author-metadata elements
(&lt;orcid&gt;, &lt;email&gt;).*

<section #ag-article-subtitle | `<article-subtitle>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<article-subtitle>`.

<section #ag-article-title | `<article-title>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<article-title>`.

<section #ag-author | `<author>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<author>`.

<code #code:ag-author-1>
<author | Jane Goodall>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-author-1>
<author | Jane Goodall>
</minipage>

*Backward-compatible casual form (carried forward from before the
structured-interface reconciliation). The pipe content sits as
text content of &lt;author&gt;; it is NOT lifted to a &lt;name&gt; child —
authors who want the structured shape use the kwarg form below
or the child-tag form. JATS export reads the name string either
way.*

<section #ag-book-part-subtitle | `<book-part-subtitle>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<book-part-subtitle>`.

<section #ag-book-part-title | `<book-part-title>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<book-part-title>`.

<section #ag-book-subtitle | `<book-subtitle>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<book-subtitle>`.

<section #ag-book-title | `<book-title>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<book-title>`.

<section #ag-config | `<config>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<config>`.

<code #code:ag-config-1>
<config citation-style=author-year number-sections=true />
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-config-1>
<config citation-style=author-year number-sections=true />
</minipage>

*The authoring form for &lt;config&gt; is kwargs. Settings are read at the
discovery pass into the configuration registry; the element itself
produces no body output (it renders as an empty &lt;config&gt;).*

<section #ag-date | `<date>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<date>`.

<code #code:ag-date-1>
<date | 2024-03-15>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-date-1>
<date | 2024-03-15>
</minipage>

*A bare &lt;date&gt; is UNTYPED (no data-date-type) — an authoring date is
"when you wrote it" (like the date on a letter), not a publication
date (cf. Quarto/Pandoc/Bookdown preamble date slots). Use an explicit
type= (e.g. &lt;date type=publication | …&gt;) for a typed date. (#325)*

<section #ag-editor | `<editor>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<editor>`.

<code #code:ag-editor-1>
<editor | The Editor>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-editor-1>
<editor | The Editor>
</minipage>

*Casual form — the pipe content is the editor's name (text content,
not lifted to a &lt;name&gt; child), mirroring &lt;author | ...&gt;.*

<section #ag-email | `<email>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<email>`.

<code-block #code:ag-email-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
  <email | jane@example.org>
</author>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-email-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
  <email | jane@example.org>
</author>
</minipage>

*Author contact email. Common in journal article metadata for
the corresponding author (see also the +corresponding boolean
kwarg on &lt;author&gt;).*

<section #ag-keywords | `<keywords>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<keywords>`.

<code-block #code:ag-keywords-1>
<meta>
  <keywords | elephants, conservation, climate, carbon storage>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-keywords-1>
<meta>
  <keywords | elephants, conservation, climate, carbon storage>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Comma-separated keyword list — the simpler and more common
authoring form. The exporter splits on commas when emitting JATS.*

<section #ag-lang | `<lang>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<lang>`.

<code-block #code:ag-lang-1>
<meta>
  <lang | en-US>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-lang-1>
<meta>
  <lang | en-US>
</meta>
</minipage>

*BCP 47 language tag. The eHTML form preserves the value as a
child element of &lt;meta&gt;; downstream consumers (the JATS exporter,
the render-mode lowering) project it where each format expects.*

<section #ag-license | `<license>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<license>`.

<code-block #code:ag-license-1>
<meta>
  <license href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" | CC BY 4.0>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-license-1>
<meta>
  <license href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" | CC BY 4.0>
</meta>
</minipage>

*License name with canonical URL.*

<section #ag-meta | `<meta>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<meta>`.

<code-block #code:ag-meta-1>
<meta type=article>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
  <date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-meta-1>
<meta type=article>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
  <date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins.
</minipage>

*Author writes &lt;meta type=article&gt; at the top with no &lt;article&gt;
wrapper. The structural plugin reads type=article and generates:
  - the &lt;article&gt; container
  - &lt;article-front&gt; wrapping the original &lt;meta&gt;
  - &lt;article-body&gt; wrapping the section content
&lt;title&gt; is promoted to &lt;article-title&gt; as the first child of &lt;meta&gt;.
&lt;meta&gt; itself survives in the output, inside &lt;article-front&gt;.*

<section #ag-name | `<name>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<name>`.

<code-block #code:ag-name-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
</author>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-name-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
</author>
</minipage>

*The common case. Pipe content becomes the name string.*

